---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { discordUrl } from '../config/site';

const contactEmail = 'Elliott@ElPlugins.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - ElPlugins"
  description="ElPlugins Privacy Policy."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        Effective 7 July 2026. Last reviewed 7 July 2026. This policy explains
        how ElPlugins handles information connected with the website, launcher,
        plugins, Discord support, purchases and related services.
      </p>

      <div class="page-actions">
        <a class="button discord-button" href={discordUrl}>Contact Us on Discord</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tos-page">
      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>

        <p>
          ElPlugins is a trading name that provides plugin access, launcher
          access, Discord support, purchase handling and related digital
          services.
        </p>

        <p>
          Discord tickets are the official channel for privacy requests. You can
          also contact us for legal or general contact purposes at
          {' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

        <p>We may collect and process the following information:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Discord identity, username, user ID, server roles and ticket history.</li>
          <li>Purchase records, access status, package history, payment references and transaction metadata.</li>
          <li>Support messages, screenshots, attachments, logs or other information you provide in tickets.</li>
          <li>Launcher, account, key, subscription and plugin access identifiers.</li>
          <li>HWID and device identifiers used to manage licensing, access limits, resets and abuse prevention.</li>
          <li>Email address if you provide one for contact, purchase, support or legal purposes.</li>
          <li>Basic technical records such as hosting, security or server logs needed to operate and protect the services.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>

        <p>We use information to:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Provide, verify and manage purchases, roles, subscriptions, keys, launcher access and plugin access.</li>
          <li>Operate HWID limits, device binding, resets, abuse checks and fraud prevention.</li>
          <li>Answer support tickets, investigate issues and manage complaints or disputes.</li>
          <li>Maintain, secure, troubleshoot and improve the services.</li>
          <li>Enforce our Terms of Service and protect ElPlugins, customers and staff.</li>
          <li>Keep records for legal, tax, accounting, chargeback, fraud prevention and dispute purposes.</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations or respond to valid requests from authorities where required.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>4. Payments and Third-Party Services</h2>

        <p>
          Payments and service delivery may involve third-party providers,
          including Discord, Stripe or other payment providers, store providers,
          hosting providers and cryptocurrency networks. These services may
          process information under their own privacy terms.
        </p>

        <p>
          We do not intentionally collect full card numbers or full bank details
          through our own website. Payment providers process those details where
          required for the payment method you choose.
        </p>

        <p>
          Cryptocurrency transactions may be recorded on public blockchain
          networks. In-game currency payments may require manual verification
          through support or store processes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>5. Analytics, Cookies and Logs</h2>

        <p>
          We do not intentionally use analytics cookies or tracking for the
          website. Essential hosting, security and server logs may still be
          created automatically when you visit the site or use related services.
        </p>

        <p>
          Third-party services, including Discord, payment providers and store
          providers, may use their own cookies, logs or tracking technologies
          according to their own policies.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>6. Sharing Information</h2>

        <p>
          We may share information where needed with service providers that help
          us operate the services, including payment processors, Discord, store
          providers, hosting providers, support tools and security providers.
        </p>

        <p>
          We may also share information where required to enforce our terms,
          prevent fraud or abuse, resolve payment disputes, comply with law, or
          protect ElPlugins, customers, staff or third parties.
        </p>

        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>7. Retention</h2>

        <p>
          We keep information only as long as reasonably needed for access,
          support, records, fraud prevention, legal, tax, accounting, security
          and dispute purposes.
        </p>

        <p>
          Some information may need to be retained after access ends, including
          purchase records, payment references, enforcement records, support
          history and records needed for disputes, chargebacks, fraud prevention
          or legal compliance.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>8. Security</h2>

        <p>
          We use reasonable measures intended to protect information connected
          with the services. No online service, storage system or transmission
          method can be guaranteed completely secure.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for keeping your Discord account, email account,
          device, launcher access and any keys or credentials secure.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>9. Your Choices and Requests</h2>

        <p>
          You may request access, correction or deletion of personal information
          by opening a Discord ticket. We may need to verify your identity and
          may refuse or limit a request where we need to keep information for
          legal, payment, fraud prevention, security, access-record or dispute
          purposes.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you ask us to delete information needed to provide access, support,
          licensing or abuse prevention, you may lose access to some or all
          services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>10. Children and Minors</h2>

        <p>
          The services are intended for users who are at least 13 years old.
          Minors must have permission from, and be supervised by, a parent or
          guardian.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you believe a child has provided information in breach of this
          policy or our Terms of Service, open a Discord ticket so we can review
          the issue.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>11. International Use</h2>

        <p>
          The services and third-party providers may process information in
          different countries. By using the services, you understand that
          information may be transferred, stored or processed outside your
          location where our providers or systems operate.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>

        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updated versions
          take effect when posted unless we state a later date. Continuing to use
          the services after changes are posted means you accept the updated
          policy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>13. Contact Us</h2>

        <p>
          For privacy requests, open a Discord ticket:
          {' '}
          <a href={discordUrl}>{discordUrl}</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          For legal or contact purposes, email
          {' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>

        <p>ElPlugins</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />

  <style>
    .tos-page {
      padding: 70px 6vw 90px;
      display: grid;
      gap: 20px;
      max-width: 1160px;
    }

    .tos-card {
      padding: 30px;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(255, 216, 74, 0.09), transparent 18rem),
        linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(36, 31, 19, 0.88), rgba(16, 14, 9, 0.95));
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .tos-card h2 {
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.4vw, 2.1rem);
    }

    .tos-card p,
    .tos-card li {
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.72;
    }

    .tos-card a {
      color: var(--gold-bright);
      font-weight: 900;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 4px;
    }

    .tos-card ul {
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      padding-left: 20px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      .tos-page {
        padding-left: 22px;
        padding-right: 22px;
      }

      .tos-card {
        padding: 24px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
